@page "/profiles"

<PageTitle>Draft vs Submit</PageTitle>
<h1>Draft vs Submit profiles</h1>
<p>One validator holds two profiles (named selections of its rules): <strong>Save draft</strong> checks only <strong>Title</strong>'s length, and <strong>Submit</strong> also requires both fields. So a draft saves with <strong>Summary</strong> empty, while a submit is blocked until <strong>Summary</strong> is filled in.</p>

<TeachingPanel CodeFiles="@(new[] { "DraftedBrief.cs", "Profiles.razor", "Profiles.razor.cs" })">
    <TryIt>
        <ol>
            <li>Look at the <strong>Title</strong> and <strong>Summary</strong> labels before typing anything.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> an asterisk beside each.</div></li>
            <li>Type more than 60 characters into <strong>Title</strong> and leave the field.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Title is 60 characters max".</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Save draft</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Draft blocked by format rules: Title is 60 characters max" in the status line.</div></li>
            <li>Shorten <strong>Title</strong> to 60 characters or fewer, then click <strong>Save draft</strong> again.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Draft saved", with <strong>Summary</strong> still empty and still marked.</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> <strong>Save draft</strong> checks only the <code>Draft</code> profile, which holds no required rules.</div></li>
            <li>Clear <strong>Title</strong> and leave the field.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Title is required to submit", with no submit pressed, while <strong>Summary</strong> stays silent.</div></li>
            <li>Type something into <strong>Summary</strong> and leave the field.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> <strong>Summary</strong> turns green.</div></li>
            <li>Clear <strong>Summary</strong> and leave the field.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> <strong>Summary</strong> shows no message, no red border and no entry in the error summary.</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> <strong>Summary</strong>'s input sets <code>WaitForSubmit="true"</code>, so it stays quiet until you press <strong>Submit</strong>.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Submit</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Summary is required to submit" under the field, joining <strong>Title</strong>'s entry in the error summary.</div></li>
            <li>Type something into <strong>Summary</strong> and leave the field.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> <strong>Summary</strong>'s message and its entry in the error summary clear, with no second submit.</div></li>
            <li>Click an entry in the error summary.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> focus moves to the field it names.</div></li>
            <li>Fill in both fields and click <strong>Submit</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Submitted" in the status line.</div></li>
            <li>Make <strong>Title</strong> longer than 60 characters and leave the field.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> "Title is 60 characters max" again.</div></li>
            <li>Click <strong>Reset</strong>.<div class="teaching__result"><span class="teaching__label">You see:</span> the message clears, but the long title stays in the box.</div><div class="teaching__why"><span class="teaching__label">Why:</span> <strong>Reset</strong> calls <code>ResetAsync()</code>, which clears the form's state but never writes a model property.</div></li>
        </ol>
    </TryIt>
    <Rules>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Title</strong>: 60 characters max, even in a draft; required to submit.</li>
            <li><strong>Summary</strong>: required to submit.</li>
        </ul>
    </Rules>
    <HowItWorks>
        <p>The two buttons ask the same validator different questions:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>A draft save asks the <code>Draft</code> profile, which holds the format rule: <strong>Title</strong> is 60 characters max. Every check runs this rule, so a draft with a long title is blocked.</li>
            <li>A submit asks the <code>Submit</code> profile, which adds the completeness rules: <strong>Title</strong> and <strong>Summary</strong> are required. A draft save skips them, so a draft saves with <strong>Summary</strong> empty.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>As you edit, the form checks your changes against the <code>Submit</code> profile's rules. <strong>Title</strong> shows its messages once you have changed it, which is why clearing it shows "Title is required to submit" with no submit pressed. A field you have never changed stays quiet however badly its rule is failing.</p>
        <p><strong>Summary</strong>'s input sets <code>WaitForSubmit="true"</code>. Changing the field still runs its rule, so a passing value turns green. A failing value gets no message, no red border and no entry in the error summary until you press <strong>Submit</strong>. From then on <strong>Summary</strong> answers your edits like <strong>Title</strong>, until <strong>Reset</strong> starts the wait again.</p>
        <p>The asterisk on each label comes from the validator. The page places a <code>FormidableRequiredIndicator</code> (the component that draws the mark) beside each label, but never says which fields are required. The indicator asks what the <code>Submit</code> profile demands, and both fields carry a <code>NotEmpty()</code> rule there. Remove a field's <code>NotEmpty()</code> and its mark goes with it.</p>
        <p>The glyph is <code>aria-hidden</code> and the input carries <code>aria-required</code>, so a screen reader is told the field is required instead of being read a star.</p>
        <p><strong>Reset</strong> calls the form's <code>ResetAsync()</code>, which keeps the same model instance. It clears which fields you have touched and changed, every message, and the form's has-submitted flag. It never writes a model property, so whatever you typed stays in the boxes.</p>
        <p>For a profile of your own beyond these two, see <a href="custom-profiles">Custom profiles</a>.</p>
    </HowItWorks>
    <Demo>
        <FormidableForm @ref="_form" Model="_brief" OnValidSubmit="HandleValid">
            <div class="summary-slot">
                <FormidableSummary />
            </div>

            <div class="field"><label>Title <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _brief.Title" /> <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_brief.Title" /></label>
                <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _brief.Title" /></div>
            <div class="field"><label>Summary <FormidableRequiredIndicator For="() => _brief.Summary" /> <FormidableInputText @bind-Value="_brief.Summary" WaitForSubmit="true" /></label>
                <FormidableFieldMessage For="() => _brief.Summary" /></div>

            <div class="actions">
                <button type="submit">Submit</button>
                <button type="button" @onclick="SaveDraft">Save draft</button>
                <button type="button" @onclick="Reset">Reset</button>
            </div>
        </FormidableForm>

        <p role="status">@_status</p>
    </Demo>
</TeachingPanel>
